  "design_notes": [
    "Section title: \"Power system (upper stage / spacecraft / capsule)\". Section 7.2.1 says the satellite reuses this table for power storage.",
    "The table has no number for cost, mass, power or reliability. \"Cheap\", \"low power\", \"high power\" and \"very expensive\" therefore cannot affect cost or the power balance yet; Core has nothing to compute from. Open design question.",
    "The \"Fact\" column is stored in twin. Li-ion + body solar shows none. F11 (solar constant) and F14 (a third of a LEO orbit in shadow) match the deployable arrays, F33 the RTG.",
    "RTG \"+60 days approvals\" is a modifier that adds 60 days to the schedule. The design does not say whether approvals run in parallel with procurement (a lead time) or after it; schedule_days is the neutral reading.",
    "RTG \"deep space only\" is read as the contracts that leave Earth orbit, C6 and C7; the Best for column names only C7. The other options carry no contracts list: Best for is advice, not a restriction.",
    "Deployable arrays: \"Deployment risk\" is the solar_array_stuck failure mode of 8.4, which MG-15 mitigates. The design gives no reliability to roll against.",
    "\"Eclipse drain (~35 of every ~90 min in LEO)\" stays in the drawback text and a flag. The two durations are orbit facts, not part figures, and have no data field."
  ],
